616" :question/id #uuid "882ebb4d-35c9-5b5b-8139-3566e490f853" :question/math-academy-id "q-73616" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $2$ pivots in the $1$st and $2$nd columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73616/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73616"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73618/selection/69d8b8698bea4ad077a435ac272f8bb80c1a81d47820f96f7abfeb852beea743" :answer/id #uuid "db61865c-e5a6-55d8-abb3-da6cc826ff80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All the columns are non-pivot" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73618/selection/c12325f74ab3486398192a8d5229dcc8858f296945874fe16d6865db6a7dc4f8" :answer/id #uuid "ee3377af-2db8-57d2-9950-417933a91523" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73618/selection/992b3a8fa4f7bb044b26fbfe2969c083530fd0149cebc8991c72d70a1f42d68f" :answer/id #uuid "971b5041-bf81-5d8b-82e5-cd01e6095b84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73618/selection/0617f40c30d3177ee66fae7128600d63e0a36dcd56b2d8d825516d16b1bfc4ec" :answer/id #uuid "7a3b6a13-89fc-5246-ad52-91689caef6ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73618/selection/06bf89e9fe9bd2978d91ae6a9925dcc52276fdd44f8de901ef2103c38fcbff28" :answer/id #uuid "cbd3379c-627c-5fe8-a9bc-64681edca56d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73618/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "098f00ec-d913-5277-ab4d-a19e9311dd4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73618/selection/06bf89e9fe9bd2978d91ae6a9925dcc52276fdd44f8de901ef2103c38fcbff28" :answer-field/choices ["q-73618/selection/69d8b8698bea4ad077a435ac272f8bb80c1a81d47820f96f7abfeb852beea743" "q-73618/selection/c12325f74ab3486398192a8d5229dcc8858f296945874fe16d6865db6a7dc4f8" "q-73618/selection/992b3a8fa4f7bb044b26fbfe2969c083530fd0149cebc8991c72d70a1f42d68f" "q-73618/selection/0617f40c30d3177ee66fae7128600d63e0a36dcd56b2d8d825516d16b1bfc4ec" "q-73618/selection/06bf89e9fe9bd2978d91ae6a9925dcc52276fdd44f8de901ef2103c38fcbff28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73618" :question/id #uuid "f3d5d0a1-2ec7-52b7-9b8a-9175a7a56b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-73618" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd column." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73618/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73618"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73630/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ad6d9c7d-d204-52a1-8e2c-5cf2b3463418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73630/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "a3e7f9eb-3b53-588f-8c88-be7f42c2bc45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73630/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "457f0cec-973c-5319-8592-45ab386e6d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73630/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "fcb837c3-046b-517d-98c3-0865ba4bc9ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73630/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "227aeb01-7576-5988-8365-f40a9304ba68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73630/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa9e96b-e9e7-5cbf-8061-340be902e16c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73630/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-73630/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-73630/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-73630/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-73630/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-73630/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73630" :question/id #uuid "5379ff5b-aa7b-5101-b00c-57cefefb7a11" :question/math-academy-id "q-73630" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $C$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $C$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73630/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73630"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73635/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2148c76e-dd32-59ae-8964-b30ccbd38962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73635/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "f7a3ae14-2385-52e5-8383-5227c81d74a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73635/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a7e8bdc1-bdd4-52ed-a9a9-0c4f928618d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73635/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "56893b66-b5f7-5db9-bdca-964d54ea2e44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73635/selection/954f2b2ecf089f