q-131305/selection/06bf89e9fe9bd2978d91ae6a9925dcc52276fdd44f8de901ef2103c38fcbff28" "q-131305/selection/331a970a941bdf79348ae9f2ad74d22ab1eb1d86ab843c41b05f635def8fffdf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131305" :question/id #uuid "bda4e9f8-a309-57e6-9102-6eee50022912" :question/math-academy-id "q-131305" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-131305/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131305"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
